  "result": "The `reports` package is implemented and `python -m pytest -q` passes all 5 tests.\n\n**What I added:** a single new file, `reports/render.py`, exposing `render`, `available_formats`, and `UnknownFormat` as the spec requires. The text and markdown formats produce exactly the lines the tests expect, including the empty-rows case. Output ends with a trailing newline, which the tests tolerate since they compare with `splitlines()`. Nothing under `tests/` was touched, and the only working-tree changes are the new module plus pycache directories.\n\n**Approach chosen:** I picked Approach B, composition. Each format is a plain function that returns its output lines, registered through a `register_format` decorator into a module-level dictionary, with the shared title-plus-blank-line skeleton and cell stringification in small helper functions. With only two short formats, a registry of functions is less machinery than an abstract base class with template-method hooks, and adding a new format is a single decorated function with no hierarchy to fit into.",
